# Changelog

## 1.3.0 — work-in-progress checkpoint

### Added
- `/api/v1/auth/login` endpoint for OIDC PKCE authentication flow
- `/api/v1/auth/callback` endpoint for handling Keycloak redirect
- `/api/v1/auth/logout` endpoint for session termination
- Frontend `Callback` page for processing auth callbacks
- Demo mode authentication flow (bypasses Keycloak for local development)
- HttpOnly cookie support for secure token storage
- PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) implementation for OIDC flow

### Changed
- Updated `main.py` to include auth router
- Updated `App.tsx` with `/callback` route
- Updated `Login.tsx` to handle demo mode redirects
- Updated `useAuth.tsx` hook for demo mode compatibility
- Updated `client.ts` with `withCredentials: true` for HttpOnly cookies
- Enhanced test parser `_last_meaningful_line` to detect more summary formats (added keywords: success, failure, skipped, ignored, pending, total, time:, finished in)

### Fixed
- Auth login endpoint missing (frontend redirected to non-existent endpoint)
- Demo mode auth flow now functional end-to-end
- Frontend 401 handling redirects to login page
- Test parser summary detection for Jest, Vitest, Cargo, Go test formats

### Security
- HttpOnly cookies for session management (production)
- PKCE for OIDC authorization code flow
- Demo mode refused in production (via `effective_demo_mode` property)
- No hardcoded secrets; all credentials via environment variables
- Frontend tokens in memory only, no localStorage persistence

### Known Limitations
- SQLite only; PostgreSQL recommended for production
- Agent Teams orchestration API stubbed; requires CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1
- LLM integration adapters not yet implemented (planned)
- Single-user demo credentials in Keycloak realm export
- Full end-to-end Docker Compose verification pending

